$ feov-record manual --help
manual prints every command on this surface — the groups, and every command they hold, in tree order — each under a header naming the command exactly, followed by the help that command prints. The help is produced now, by running this binary with that command and --help, so it cannot disagree with the tool you are running. It records nothing.

Read it ONCE, at the start of a sitting and before you decide what to do: it is your whole surface in one call. A command's own --help is still there when you want to re-check one page.

The surface is your seat's — the seat you registered as, or the one this call names. A page whose help fails to run is printed with its error, never left out, and the command then exits non-zero.

